# This repository is public: anything committed can be read by anyone, and it
# stays in the git history after it is deleted. Keep keys and local files out.
# Your app's keys live in Pippa (Apps > Created by me > your app > Keys); a
# local copy goes in `.env`. `.env.example` lists the names with no values,
# and is the one that is committed.
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
# Copies of .env under other names: an editor's backup (.env~), what Windows
# names a copied file (.env - Copy), .env-prod, .env_local, direnv's .envrc.
.env~
.env *
.env-*
.env_*
.envrc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
credentials*.json
secrets.json
.netrc
.pypirc
.claude/settings.local.json
env/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
